<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Constantine I of Greece</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1868">1868</a>–<a href="/years/1923">1923</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-i">Constantine I</a> was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> from 1913 to 1917 and from 1920 to 1922. A successful commander in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkan-wars">Balkan Wars</a>, he insisted on neutrality in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, which brought him into conflict with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eleftherios-venizelos">Eleftherios Venizelos</a> and led to the National Schism. Forced out in 1917, he returned after an election in 1920 but abdicated again after the defeat in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a> in 1922.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constantine-i-of-greece.jpg" alt="Constantine I of Greece" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Harris &amp;amp; Ewing Collection · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Constantine_I_of_Greece_in_1914.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
